user: Why is the agent-runner trying to automatically load a new model, when there is an active one already? Instead, in order to expedite access and speed. Start with the currently active model. Then there is no model switching cost, and we can get to work a lot faster. If the currently active model is not configured for the agent-runner, then offer to do so.
However, if there is no active model, then do load the default one, if there is a default and that makes sense. The model choice typically depends on the prompt that the user wishes to run, therefore it might actually not be a good idea to have a default, in case more than one is configured. I.e. the default should be the currently active model. Then if there is only a single choice configured we could automatically load it, if there was no active model already, as a convenience to the user since we know that's likely the correct choice then. Otherwise, delay loading a model until the user has selected one, if none were already active.
