Ollama's `/api/tags` lists all models on disk, and `/api/ps` lists loaded models.

So the "currently active model" is discoverable from both providers.

Now, why does the agent-runner "auto-load a new model"? Because the model selector at startup is purely static: `--model` override, else `default_model` in config. It never consults what's loaded on the provider. If a user has started llama-server with model A and the config's default_model points to model B, the agent-runner will send requests to B, and the provider will load/switch (incurring the switch cost), and with Ollama it might even try to pull from the registry (though the network is presumably denied in this sandbox).

