tool stdout: commit de06a7c0393a325bb4a3b20da3dc331b34fedee4
Author: Stefan Lindblad <stefan.lindblad@linux.com>
Date:   Sat Oct 3 14:03:06 2026 +0200

    fix(agent_runner): launch without model delay and fix reported TUI issues
    
    The terminal UI now appears immediately: transport setup and the provider connection/model load run on a background bootstrap thread, the first prompt is held and dispatched when the worker is ready, and a failed bootstrap is a non-fatal notice the next submission recovers from. Submitting with a changed model or effort cancels the old worker, discards its stale bootstrap and starts a new one with the held prompt. The slot-allocation (model load/switch) and time-to-first-token (long-prompt prefill) watchdogs each get the full per-turn deadline, so a slow model switch completes within the turn instead of hitting a short fixed timeout and killing the run; the inter-token cadence watchdog still catches post-first-token stalls.
    
    The ESC menu now closes on selection: a history item opens the replay overlay and "New session" (Enter or n) starts a fresh session. Ctrl+N starts a new session from anywhere (it previously advanced prompt history; Ctrl+P keeps backward history navigation).
    
    Session records are named session-{UTC date-time}-{pid}-{n} and, after the first prompt, both journal and transcript are atomically renamed to append a bounded slug of its first words, so transcripts are recognisable by content.
    
    Limits are now safety bounds, not expected runtimes: the TUI prompt cap rises from 16,384 to 1,048,576 characters, the turn cap from 50 to 500, the wall budget from 30 minutes to 24 hours and the estimated token budget from 1M to 100M, so long prompts run uninterrupted to a result, a detected hang/loop, or a real failure.
    
    Every transcript row now fills the box's inner width (border excluded) so blocks read as enclosed textboxes: prompt echo, reasoning and agent-produced content carry distinct subtle backgrounds, with single-line tool rows sharing the agent background.
    
    Updates CONTRACT.md, DESIGN.md and REQUIREMENTS.md to match. New tests cover the slug bounds, rename-once semantics and the worker on_prompt failure path; the slug tests exposed and fixed a double hyphen and a 41-character overflow.

