provider reasoning: Now, let's take a look at how the TUI handles model switching in app.rs, and understand the concept of "active model". The user's premise is that "the agent runner tries to automatically load a new model even though there's already an active one."

In other words, in agent-runner (this workspace's own tool), the flow is as follows:
1. `default_model` is required in the configuration
2. At startup, it immediately boots a bootstrap worker for that model (transport, etc.)
3. The provider (llama-server / Ollama) loads the model when a request comes in — model switching takes time.

Therefore, when you run agent-runner, even if a model that is already "active" (i.e., already loaded into the llama-server process) is a different model, agent-runner will always start the default model from the configuration — so it ends up switching the provider's loaded model. If the user has, for example, a 35B model loaded in llama-server and then starts agent-runner which uses default_model = qwen... the provider switches the loaded model, causing a big delay.

