1. What I found (current behavior, code references).
2. Why it looks like it "auto-loads a new model" (mechanics: default_model is required, selected at startup, provider load/switch is expected and bounded by the turn's deadline; the runner has no concept of the provider's active model — the plumbing to read it exists (Ollama's /api/ps, llama-server's /props and /v1/models) but is only used for capacity).
3. Assessment of the user's proposal — I agree; refined priority order; nuance for headless; the default_model semantics change; the suggestion to offer configuration; matching by provider name.
4. Suggested concrete design (rules + where to implement + caveats: test mocks, contract docs, multi-provider ambiguity, non-fatal probe, explicit wins).
5. Conclusion: yes, it makes sense and it's more intuitive.

